The directory upstream/ is that commit's Dockerfile, LICENSE, and scripts,
copied without modification. The upstream keys/ directory is not vendored.
ADB keys are created at runtime or mounted from outside git.

Open5G changes are patches/0001-open5g-boot.patch and open5g-preflight.sh.
build.sh copies upstream/, applies the patch, and builds the image from this
repository. The patch pins the base image and the Android command-line tools
checksum, removes the ADB key copy, listens for adb on loopback only, and
runs a read-only preflight before QEMU.

Do not push the built image to a public registry. The SDK install accepts
the Android SDK and Google licenses inside the image.
